ve time to do a whole lot of damage  before the ghostbusters managed to  essentially roast him but he does crash  through a good portion of manhattan and  the resulting marshmallow group covers  quite a bit at fifth avenue by the time  it's all over the whole city and by  extension the whole country saw what  happened so what did the owners of stay  puft do in response to this do they put  out a statement clarifying that they had  no involvement in their mascot's hijinks  when you're an adult who's very used to  brands making various plays for  attention it becomes a question worth  asking  ghostbusters doesn't spend all that much  time breaking down how the system of  ghost capture and control actually works  but we do get a glimpse into what  happens to the spirits after the boys  bust them as rey explains to winston  they put the trapped ghost into their  specially designed storage facility  which is basically some kind of  electronic grid that stores a ghost in a  secure way what the film doesn't ever  explore is what if anything the ghosts  actually think or feel about their new  home the ghosts we see over the course  of the film at least some of the time  appear to be semi-sentient creatures and  many of them appear to be mischievous  but not outright evil is it for lack of  a better word humane to keep them all  trapped in there can they feel it  some of the ghosts and ghostbusters seem  like genuinely terrifying beings that no  one would want to be around while others  seem a bit more quirky and less prone to  actually inflicting harm on anyone still  to the ghostbusters they all seem to  just be another form of past like  roaches or silverfish their job isn't to  reason with a ghost or to judge them or  even to separate the bad ones from the  relatively good they just seem to be  trapping them and storing them in their  special grid from a kid's point of view  this probably makes sense but watching  the film as an adult you may get the  overwhelming sense 